From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 08:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] zfs: allocate the ARC eviction waiter on the identity
 heap for OSv fork

arc_wait_for_eviction() declared its arc_evict_waiter_t on the calling
thread's stack. On OSv with fork() emulation a process runs in its own
copy-on-write address space, so that stack (and the embedded kcondvar_t
aew_cv, whose OSv condvar holds a lockfree mutex and a waiter FIFO) is
COW-private to the forked process. The process links the waiter onto the
process-global arc_evict_waiters list and cv_waits; the AS0 arc_evict thread
later runs arc_evict_cb -> cv_signal(&aw->aew_cv) -> condvar wake,
dereferencing the forked process's stack-resident condvar through AS0's page
tables. AS0 sees a physically different, incoherent copy, so the wake either
faults on a stale/null waiter pointer or is silently dropped and the process
that is waiting for ARC eviction never wakes. This blocked concurrent forked
processes under ARC write pressure.

Allocate the waiter with kmem_zalloc, which under OSv's fork support routes to
the identity kernel heap that is mapped verbatim in every address space, so
the waiting process and the AS0 evictor operate on the same physical aew_cv /
aew_node / aew_count. ARC is a process-global kernel singleton and this waiter
is signalled by an AS0 thread, so the identity heap is its correct home.
Semantics are unchanged: the list_link_active(&aw->aew_node) real-vs-spurious
wakeup check still works, against a coherent node.
---
 module/zfs/arc.c | 20 ++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/module/zfs/arc.c b/module/zfs/arc.c
--- a/module/zfs/arc.c
+++ b/module/zfs/arc.c
@@ -5175,9 +5218,24 @@ arc_wait_for_eviction(uint64_t amount, boolean_t lax, boolean_t use_reserve)
 	case ARC_OVF_SEVERE:
 	default:
 	{
-		arc_evict_waiter_t aw;
-		list_link_init(&aw.aew_node);
-		cv_init(&aw.aew_cv, NULL, CV_DEFAULT, NULL);
+		/*
+		 * OSv fork COW-coherence: the waiter must NOT live on this
+		 * thread's stack.  Under CONF_fork a PostgreSQL backend runs in
+		 * its own copy-on-write address space, so a stack object is
+		 * physically private to that AS.  The ARC eviction thread runs
+		 * in AS0 and signals aew_cv / walks aew_node cross-AS from
+		 * arc_evict_cb(); a COW-private stack copy makes those touch a
+		 * different physical page than the waiter -> the embedded
+		 * condvar's internal mutex is incoherent and cv_signal ->
+		 * condvar_wake_one -> mutex::lock either NULL-derefs (page fault
+		 * via taskqueue_thread_loop) or drops the wakeup (all vCPUs idle,
+		 * the DB wedges under VU>=4).  kmem_zalloc routes to the identity
+		 * kernel heap (mapped verbatim in every AS) under fork, so the
+		 * waiter is coherent for both the backend and the AS0 evictor.
+		 */
+		arc_evict_waiter_t *aw = kmem_zalloc(sizeof (*aw), KM_SLEEP);
+		list_link_init(&aw->aew_node);
+		cv_init(&aw->aew_cv, NULL, CV_DEFAULT, NULL);
 
 		uint64_t last_count = 0;
 		mutex_enter(&arc_evict_lock);
@@ -5194,16 +5252,16 @@ arc_wait_for_eviction(uint64_t amount, boolean_t lax, boolean_t use_reserve)
 		 * case arc_evict_state_impl() may have deferred
 		 * wakeups (but still incremented arc_evict_count).
 		 */
-		aw.aew_count = MAX(last_count, arc_evict_count) + amount;
+		aw->aew_count = MAX(last_count, arc_evict_count) + amount;
 
-		list_insert_tail(&arc_evict_waiters, &aw);
+		list_insert_tail(&arc_evict_waiters, aw);
 
 		arc_set_need_free();
 
 		DTRACE_PROBE3(arc__wait__for__eviction,
 		    uint64_t, amount,
 		    uint64_t, arc_evict_count,
-		    uint64_t, aw.aew_count);
+		    uint64_t, aw->aew_count);
 
 		/*
 		 * We will be woken up either when arc_evict_count reaches
@@ -5212,11 +5270,12 @@ arc_wait_for_eviction(uint64_t amount, boolean_t lax, boolean_t use_reserve)
 		 * In case of "false" wakeup, we will still be on the list.
 		 */
 		do {
-			cv_wait(&aw.aew_cv, &arc_evict_lock);
-		} while (list_link_active(&aw.aew_node));
+			cv_wait(&aw->aew_cv, &arc_evict_lock);
+		} while (list_link_active(&aw->aew_node));
 		mutex_exit(&arc_evict_lock);
 
-		cv_destroy(&aw.aew_cv);
+		cv_destroy(&aw->aew_cv);
+		kmem_free(aw, sizeof (*aw));
 	}
 	}
 }
